## Factual differences

- `safe_l2`, `finalized_l2`, `local_safe_l2`:
  - LightCL: all-zero BlockRef (hash `0x00…0`, number 0, timestamp 0, l1origin zero)
  - Sequencer: number 0, hash `0x30138b…`, timestamp 1776955116, l1origin number 10716997
- `head_l1`, `safe_l1`, `finalized_l1`, `current_l1_finalized`: populated on both.
- `unsafe_l2`, `cross_unsafe_l2`: populated on both.
- `current_l1`: zero on both.
- `pending_safe_l2`: zero on both.

## Environment

- Fresh-genesis OP chain.
- LightCL uses `--l2.follow.source` pointing at another op-node on the same chain.
- Both nodes otherwise functioning: unsafe chain is advancing on both.

## What I don't know

Whether this reflects a bug in follow-source mode, an expected initialization phase, or something else. Filed for visibility.

## Related

- #20294 — separate LightCL / follow-source concern on op-node restart.
